---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service | NodeAuth" description="NodeAuth Terms of Service">
    <div class="legal-container">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: September 2026</p>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <p>By accessing or using the NodeAuth.io website, mobile application, or browser extension (collectively, the "Services"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service.</p>

            <h3>Part 1: General Terms & Architecture</h3>
            <p><strong>Zero-Knowledge & Responsibilities:</strong> NodeAuth operates on a zero-knowledge, local-first architecture. We do not host your credentials or master password on our servers. <strong>You are solely responsible for safeguarding your master password and 2FA secrets.</strong> We cannot recover your data if you lose your device and have not configured a backup.</p>
            <p><strong>BYOS (Bring Your Own Server):</strong> If you utilize the BYOS feature to sync data to a custom server, you acknowledge that NodeAuth does not monitor, endorse, or secure these external servers. You assume all risks associated with transmitting data to third-party or self-hosted environments.</p>

            <h3>Part 2: Platform EULA (Mobile & Browser Extension)</h3>
            <p><strong>App Store & Web Store Disclaimer:</strong> You acknowledge that these Terms are concluded between you and NodeAuth.io, not with Apple Inc., Google LLC (including Google Play and Chrome Web Store), Microsoft Corporation, or Mozilla Corporation. These third-party entities are not responsible for the App or Extension, its content, or obligated to provide any maintenance or support services. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms, and upon your acceptance, Apple will have the right to enforce these Terms against you as a third-party beneficiary.</p>
            <p><strong>Disclaimer of Warranty:</strong> The App is provided "as is" and "as available". While we utilize industry-standard cryptographic algorithms, we do not warrant that the App will be completely immune to all potential threats, malware, or operating system vulnerabilities.</p>
            <p><strong>Limitation of Liability:</strong> In no event shall NodeAuth.io or its developers be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages, including loss of data or loss of access to your third-party accounts (lockouts) arising from your use of the App.</p>

            <h3>Part 3: Cross-Platform License & Refund Policy</h3>
            <p id="refund-policy"><strong>Digital Products Nature:</strong> NodeAuth PRO Lifetime licenses are proprietary digital goods delivered instantly upon acquisition of a cross-platform license. This section applies <strong>only</strong> to cross-platform licenses acquired outside of the App Store or Google Play and does not apply to In-App Purchases (IAP). Refunds for IAP must be requested directly through Apple or Google.</p>
            <p><strong>Usage Rights:</strong> A purchased license grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the NodeAuth software. The PRO Lifetime license is a cross-platform digital key valid for the lifetime of the product, allowing concurrent activation on up to 5 personal devices.</p>
            <p><strong>No Refund Policy:</strong> Due to the irreversible nature of digital license key issuance, <strong>all sales are final</strong>. We do not offer refunds, returns, or exchanges once a license key has been generated and dispatched to your email. Please review your order carefully before completing the payment.</p>
            <p><strong>Exceptions & Support:</strong> We will issue a full refund only in exceptional cases: (1) duplicate charges due to a payment processing error; (2) you were charged but no license was delivered and our support team is unable to resolve the issue within 5 business days. A technical issue does not qualify for a refund unless it is proven that the license provided was fundamentally defective and unresolvable.</p>
            <p><strong>Dispute Policy:</strong> If you believe a payment was made in error or did not receive your license, please contact us before initiating a chargeback. We are committed to resolving legitimate issues promptly and fairly.</p>

            <h3>Part 4: Governing Law & Contact</h3>
            <p>These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with applicable international law. We reserve the right to update these Terms at any time. For any legal or billing inquiries, please contact us at: <a href="mailto:support@nodeauth.io">support@nodeauth.io</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
.legal-container {
    padding: clamp(6rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem) clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: left;
    animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease-out forwards;
}

.legal-container h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.last-updated {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
}

.legal-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
}

.legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
}

.legal-content ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
}

.legal-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.legal-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
}

.legal-content a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
}
</style>
